the knowledge base ostomy_supplies includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base ostomy_supplies includes:

LCD L33828 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33828".
the text of LCD L33828 is at "sources/lcd/L33828.txt".
Policy Article A52487 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52487".
the text of Policy Article A52487 is at "sources/article/A52487.txt".

% The ostomy supplies: the codes of the LCD's table, and the pouches,
% barriers, faceplates, vents, filters and absorbent material the Article's
% coding guidelines describe.
rule ostomy_supply_codes with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "The quantity of ostomy supplies needed by a beneficiary is determined primarily by the type of ostomy, its location, its construction, and the condition of the skin surface surrounding the stoma":
an item is an ostomy supply
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4357", "A4361", "A4362", "A4363", "A4364", "A4366", "A4367", "A4368", "A4369", "A4371", "A4375", "A4376", "A4377", "A4378", "A4379", "A4380", "A4381", "A4382", "A4383", "A4398", "A4399", "A4402", "A4404", "A4405", "A4406", "A4407", "A4408", "A4409", "A4411", "A4412", "A4413", "A4414", "A4415", "A4416", "A4417", "A4418", "A4419", "A4420", "A4422", "A4423", "A4424", "A4425", "A4426", "A4427", "A4429", "A4431", "A4432", "A4433", "A4434", "A4435", "A4436", "A4437", "A4450", "A4452", "A4455", "A5051", "A5052", "A5053", "A5054", "A5055", "A5056", "A5057", "A5061", "A5062", "A5063", "A5071", "A5072", "A5073", "A5081", "A5082", "A5083", "A5093", "A5102", "A5120", "A5121", "A5122", "A5126", "A5131", "A6216"].

% Two supplies used one instead of the other: the liquid barrier and the
% wipes or swabs; the night drainage bag and bottle of a urinary ostomy.
% Both claims are denied: the LCD says which pair, not which of the two.
rule ostomy_liquid_barrier_or_wipes with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "When a liquid barrier is necessary, either liquid or spray (A4369) or individual wipes or swabs (A5120) are appropriate. The use of both is not reasonable and necessary":
an item conflicts with a concurrent ostomy supply
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4369", "A5120"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is an other code
    and the other code is in ["A4369", "A5120"]
    and the other code is different from the code.

rule ostomy_night_drainage with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "Beneficiaries with urinary ostomies may use either a bag (A4357) or bottle (A5102) for drainage at night. It is not reasonable and necessary to have both":
an item conflicts with a concurrent ostomy supply
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4357", "A5102"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and an other item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the other item is an other code
    and the other code is in ["A4357", "A5102"]
    and the other code is different from the code.

% The diagnosis code of the claim, read against the Article's table.
rule ostomy_diagnosis_code with provenance Policy Article A52487,
        confer "Ostomy supplies are appropriately used for colostomies, ileostomies or urinary ostomies (see covered diagnosis codes below.)":
the diagnosis code of a beneficiary is a covered ostomy diagnosis code
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52487" as a description under table ostomy_icd10.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides — the ostomy supplies — and their benefit:
% the Prosthetic Device benefit (Policy Article A52487), with no condition
% on the place of use.
rule ostomy_codes with provenance Policy Article A52487,
        confer "Ostomy supplies are covered under the Prosthetic Device benefit (Social Security Act Section 1861(s)(8))":
the policy for code a code is ostomy_supplies
    if the code is in ["A4357", "A4361", "A4362", "A4363", "A4364", "A4366", "A4367", "A4368", "A4369", "A4371", "A4375", "A4376", "A4377", "A4378", "A4379", "A4380", "A4381", "A4382", "A4383", "A4398", "A4399", "A4402", "A4404", "A4405", "A4406", "A4407", "A4408", "A4409", "A4411", "A4412", "A4413", "A4414", "A4415", "A4416", "A4417", "A4418", "A4419", "A4420", "A4422", "A4423", "A4424", "A4425", "A4426", "A4427", "A4429", "A4431", "A4432", "A4433", "A4434", "A4435", "A4436", "A4437", "A4450", "A4452", "A4455", "A5051", "A5052", "A5053", "A5054", "A5055", "A5056", "A5057", "A5061", "A5062", "A5063", "A5071", "A5072", "A5073", "A5081", "A5082", "A5083", "A5093", "A5102", "A5120", "A5121", "A5122", "A5126", "A5131", "A6216"].

section applicability is:

rule ostomy_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52487,
        confer "Ostomy supplies are covered under the Prosthetic Device benefit (Social Security Act Section 1861(s)(8))":
the benefit category of code a code is prosthetic devices
    if the policy for code the code is ostomy_supplies.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Every supply: within the usual maximum quantity (or the excess explained),
% and not beside the supply it replaces.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ostomy_supplies_covered with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "The actual quantity needed for a particular beneficiary may be more or less than the amount listed depending on the factors that affect the frequency of barrier and pouch change":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an ostomy supply
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the claim is within the usual maximum quantity of ostomy supplies
    and it is not the case that
        the item conflicts with a concurrent ostomy supply.

rule ostomy_usual_quantity with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "The explanation for use of a greater quantity of supplies than the amounts listed must be clearly documented in the beneficiary’s medical record":
a claim is within the usual maximum quantity of ostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the ostomy supply quantity of the claim is allowed for the beneficiary.

% the cascade decides one claim and one beneficiary at a time (both bound
% by the head): within the listed amount, otherwise the explanation
rule ostomy_quantity_allowed with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "If adequate documentation is not provided when requested, the excess quantities will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
the ostomy supply quantity of a claim is allowed for a beneficiary
    if the claim is within the listed amount of ostomy supplies
    otherwise the finding excess ostomy supplies explained about the beneficiary is established.

rule ostomy_listed_amount with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "USUAL MAXIMUM QUANTITY OF SUPPLIES":
a claim is within the listed amount of ostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the usual maximum for ostomy supply the code is a quantity under table ostomy_quantity
    and the period of the usual maximum for ostomy supply the code is a number months under table ostomy_period
    and the claim is for a supply of an other number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is a third number
    and a limit is the quantity * ceiling(the other number / the number)
    and the third number <= the limit.

% a supply the table does not list (a pouch with a convex or extended wear
% barrier, a faceplate system, a high output pouch): no usual maximum — a
% device of this model
rule ostomy_no_listed_amount:
a claim is within the listed amount of ostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the usual maximum for ostomy supply the code is a quantity under table ostomy_quantity.

section remedy is:

% The Policy Article's own conditions of payment: the permanent impairment
% requiring an ostomy, the kind of ostomy and its diagnosis code, no covered
% home health episode, the clamps as replacements, the dispensing cap of
% the LCD's refill paragraph.
% (the home health episode: "Ostomy supplies are not separately payable
% when a beneficiary is in a covered home health episode")
rule ostomy_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52487,
        confer "In addition, there are specific statutory payment policy requirements, discussed below, that also must be met":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is ostomy_supplies
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the ostomy benefit requirements
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary is in a covered home health episode
    and the ostomy clamp requirement is met for the item
    and the claim is within the dispensing limit for ostomy supplies.

% "Ostomy supplies are covered for use on a beneficiary with a surgically
% created opening (stoma) to divert urine, or fecal contents outside the
% body" — a colostomy, an ileostomy or a urinary ostomy ("Use for other
% conditions will be denied as noncovered"), permanent, with its diagnosis
% code on the claim.
rule ostomy_permanent_impairment with provenance Policy Article A52487,
        confer "Ostomy supplies are covered for a beneficiary who has a permanent impairment requiring an ostomy":
a beneficiary meets the ostomy benefit requirements
    if the ostomy of the beneficiary is a kind
    and the kind is in [colostomy, ileostomy, urinary ostomy]
    and the finding permanent impairment requiring ostomy about the beneficiary is established
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a covered ostomy diagnosis code.

% any supply other than a clamp: no condition — a device of this model
rule ostomy_not_a_clamp:
the ostomy clamp requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is "A4363".

rule ostomy_clamp_replacement with provenance Policy Article A52487,
        confer "Ostomy clamps are only payable when ordered as a replacement":
the ostomy clamp requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "A4363"
    and the item was ordered as a replacement.

rule ostomy_dispensing_nursing_facility with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "a supplier must not dispense more than a one (1) -month supply at a time for a beneficiary in a nursing facility and a three (3) -month supply for a beneficiary at home":
a claim is within the dispensing limit for ostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the residence of the beneficiary is nursing facility
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 1.

rule ostomy_dispensing_home with provenance LCD L33828,
        confer "a supplier must not dispense more than a one (1) -month supply at a time for a beneficiary in a nursing facility and a three (3) -month supply for a beneficiary at home":
a claim is within the dispensing limit for ostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the residence of the beneficiary is nursing facility
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 3.

% Continued need: once the permanent impairment is established, no further
% documentation of it (an addition to the shared continued need rules of
% dmepos.le; continued use is documented by the refill request).
rule ostomy_continued_need with provenance Policy Article A52487,
        confer "There is no requirement for further documentation of continued medical need as long as the beneficiary continues to meet the Prosthetic Devices benefit":
the continued need requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is ostomy_supplies
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the ostomy benefit requirements.
